# Examples

The repository examples are small by design. Each one isolates a language or
runtime boundary that is easy to inspect in source.

## Start with these

| Example | What it demonstrates | Run |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `counter` | Standalone state, SQLite, GET document, POST patches | `rocci run examples/counter/Counter.rocci` |
| `styling` | File-level and component-scoped `@css` | `rocci run examples/styling/Styling.rocci` |
| `rocdown` | Markdown, page metadata, Roc values, components, links | `rocdown run examples/rocdown/Guide.rocdown` |
| `rocdown` blocks | `:note`, `:tabs`, `:figure`, a wide table, and a long fence | `rocdown run examples/rocdown/Blocks.rocdown` |
| `errors` | Styled 404 and parse-error previews | `rocdown run examples/errors/ErrorDemo.rocdown` |
| `snake` | A larger standalone Rocci app | `rocci run examples/snake` |
| `datastar` | Search, edit, todos, tabs, and validation patterns | `rocci run examples/datastar` |
| `rocdown-site` | Two-page static documentation fixture | `rocdown build examples/rocdown-site --output dist` |
| `rocdown-counter` | Hybrid CDN page, SQLite count, timezone click feed | `rocdown run examples/rocdown-counter` |
| `rocdown-hybrid` | Page-kind fixture (`static` / `hydrate` / `live`) | `rocdown run examples/rocdown-hybrid` |

When working from source, prefix `rocci` with
`cargo run -q -p rocci-cli --` and `rocdown` with
`cargo run -q -p rocci-rocdown-cli --`.

## Counter

Read `examples/counter/Counter.rocci` when learning the complete standalone
flow. It creates SQLite state, serves a document, and returns the same
`CounterCard` component after increment and reset actions.

`examples/rocdown-counter` is the hybrid form of that card: Markdown on a CDN
page, colocated `@on:post` handlers, and `rocdown serve-islands` for SQLite.
See [Publish a hybrid Rocdown site](/docs/guides/hybrid-sites/).

## Datastar gallery

The gallery ports several interaction patterns while keeping server state in
Roc. It is the best place to compare `@let`, `@if`, `@for`, `@match`, and
dynamic Datastar URLs in realistic components.

## Syntax fixtures

`test/AllSyntax.rocci` and `test/AllSyntax.rocdown` intentionally exercise the
grammar more densely than a tutorial. Use them with `rocci inspect --ast` (for
`.rocci`) and `rocdown inspect ast` (for `.rocdown`) when working on parser or
source-map behavior.

